I once ran into a really strange rendering issue on Zebra EC55 devices running Android 10. 
A TextField inside a BottomSheet would randomly have its border broken — sometimes from the edge, sometimes from somewhere in the middle.
At first, I was convinced it had something to do with the layout. 
I suspected the BottomSheet padding, the TextField starting at the same position, or even another widget overlapping/clipping the border.
I tried several layout and padding changes, but nothing worked.
After a lot of trial and error, I finally tried disabling Flutter's Impeller rendering engine. And surprisingly it worked. 

Issue
Device: Zebra EC55
OS: Android 10
Framework: Flutter
UI: TextField inside BottomSheet
TextField borders were randomly breaking.
The break could appear anywhere edge or middle.


What I Tried
Checked BottomSheet padding.
Checked TextField positioning.
Changed margins and spacing.
Checked for overlapping widgets.
Checked possible clipping/layout issues.
Tried multiple UI-level changes.
Nothing fixed it.

What Finally Worked

Disabled Impeller and forced Flutter to use the Skia renderer.

<meta-data
    android:name="io.flutter.embedding.android.EnableImpeller"
    android:value="false" />

After this change, the TextField borders rendered correctly on the affected devices.

Takeaway

If you encounter a weird Flutter rendering issue that is:

Device-specific
Android-version-specific
Random/inconsistent
Not explained by the widget layout

Don't keep changing the UI endlessly.
